  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nClayton County, Iowa - County Government and Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n\n\n\n Welcome to the new website for Clayton County! More features available soon.\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n Search\n \n \n \n\n \n\n About \n \n\n Boards & Commissions\n Cemeteries\n Communities\n District Court\n Elected Officials \n News\n School Districts\n Townships\n \n \n \n\n Departments \n \n\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor\n Board of Supervisors\n Conservation\n E-911\n Emergency Management\n Engineer's Office & Secondary Roads\n Environmental Health & Zoning\n General Relief & Assistance\n Human Resources\n Medical Examiner\n Public Health\n Recorder\n Sheriff\n Solid Waste\n Treasurer\n Veterans Affairs\n \n \n \n\n Resources \n \n \n\n Bid Notices\n Calendar\n Employment Opportunites\n Facility Reservations\n FAQ\n Maps\n Notifications\n Open Record Requests\n Property Tax Resources\n Resource Guide\n \n \n \n\n Contact\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n Search Clayton County, Iowa\n \n\n \n \n \n\n Search\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nFamily Travel Nomads \n\n \n\n Explore All the County Offers\n \nWelcome to Clayton County\n \n \n\n View All Departments + Services\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n Agendas & Minutes \n \n \n\n \n \n Real Estate Search (Beacon) \n \n \n\n \n \n Pay Property Taxes \n \n \n\n \n \n Elections \n \n \n\n \n \n Renew Vehicle Tags \n \n \n\n \n \n Notifications \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Calendar\n \nMeetings + Events\n \n \nView All Events\n \n \n\n \n\n \nOctober 20\n Board of Supervisors Meeting\n 9:00 am\n Supervisors' Office, County Office Building · \n\n \nBoard of Supervisors Meeting\n Supervisors' Office, County Office Building\n 600 Gunder Rd. NE Suite 3\n Elkader, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 20, 2026 \n 9:00 am \n\nThe Board typically meets on Tuesdays with the agenda beginning at 9:00 am. Contact the Clayton County Auditor’s Office to submit agenda items (by email to [email protected] or by phone at 563-245-1106). The deadline for submitting items to be included on the agenda is 12:00 pm (noon) on the Thursday preceding the meeting. \nPosted by: Board of Supervisors \n\n \n \n \n\n \nOctober 24\n Pony Hollow Trail 5k Race\n 9:00 am\n Pony Hollow Trail · \n\n \nPony Hollow Trail 5k Race\n Pony Hollow Trail\n Elkader, IA\n \n\n October 24, 2026 \n 9:00 am \n\nClayton County Conservation invites you to the 8th Annual Pony Hollow Trail 5k on October 24, 2026. It has been decided to not do the 15k this year while the new portion of the trail is under construction. But in 2027 a whole new distance and route for the race will be announced! \n \n\n​Race swag are only guaranteed to all those that pre-register before October 12th. No extras will be ordered. All online registrations close at 1 pm on October 23rd. Mailed in registrations must also be received by Oct. 23rd.  \n \n\n5k: $25 thru Oct. 23, $30 on race day​ \n \n\nRace Bib pickup and day-of registration will be from 7:30-8:45am on race day at the Floral Hall shelter house located in the Elkader City Park. There is also parking and bathrooms located in this area for your convenience.     \n \n\nRace will start promptly at 9 AM near the south trailhead. \n \n\nNo parking will be allowed on High Street. Please use the city park, pool parking lot, or football field parking.   \nFor More Information\n \nContact: Molly \n(563) 245-1516 \n[email protected] \nWebsite\n \nPosted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \nOctober 27\n Board of Supervisors Meeting\n 9:00 am\n Supervisors' Office, County Office Building · \n\n \nBoard of Supervisors Meeting\n Supervisors' Office, County Office Building\n 600 Gunder Rd. NE Suite 3\n Elkader, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 27, 2026 \n 9:00 am \n\nThe Board typically meets on Tuesdays with the agenda beginning at 9:00 am. Contact the Clayton County Auditor’s Office to submit agenda items (by email to [email protected] or by phone at 563-245-1106). The deadline for submitting items to be included on the agenda is 12:00 pm (noon) on the Thursday preceding the meeting. \nPosted by: Board of Supervisors \n\n \n \n \n\n \nNovember 3\n General Election Day\n 7:00 am\n Assigned Polling Places · \n\n \nGeneral Election Day\n Assigned Polling Places\n Elkader, IA\n \n\n November 3, 2026 \n 7:00 am · 8:00 pm \n\nPolling places across the county are open today for voting. You must vote where you reside as absentee voting ended November 2, 2026. \nFor More Information\n \n(563) 245-1106 \n[email protected] \nWebsite\n \nPosted by: Auditor \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nNews and Announcements\n \n \n\n \nOctober 5\n \n \n\n Employment\n \n2 Job Openings\n \n \n \n \n\n \nSeptember 25\n \n \n\n Auditor\n \n2026 General Election\n \n \n \n \n\n \nAugust 28\n \n \n\n Public Health\n \nMeasles: MMR Vaccines\n \n \n \nView All News \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \nStay Informed\n \nClayton County Notifications\n \n\n \nBe the first to know about county news, bid notices, employment opportunities, and other key updates by signing up for email alerts about the topics that matter most to you. \n \n \nSubscribe\n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nAbout Clayton County\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n\nEstablished in 1837, Clayton County is a collection of 18 communities and home to over 17,000 residents. The county was named in honor of John M. Clayton, United States Senator from Delaware and later Secretary of State under President Zachary Taylor. Clayton County is administered by a three-member Board of Supervisors, who are Supervisors, who are elected for four-year terms. Other elected officials include the Attorney, Auditor, Recorder, Sheriff, and Treasurer. \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n County Courthouse\n 111 High St. NE\n \nElkader, IA 52043 \n \n\n Office Building\n 600 Gunder Rd. NE\n\n Elkader, IA 52043\n \n \n\n Hours\n M-F 8:00 am to 4:00 pm\n\n Department Hours May Vary\n \n \n\n Contact Us\n Closed Holidays \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n© 2026 Clayton County | Accessibility | Title VI\n \npowered by \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVeterans Day (November 11, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving Day (November 26, 2026)\n \nFriday after Thanksgiving (November 27, 2026)\n \nChristmas Eve Day (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas Day (December 25, 2026)\n \nNew Year’s Day (January 1, 2027)\n \nPresidents' Day (February 15, 2027)\n \nGood Friday (March 26, 2027)\n \nMemorial Day (May 31, 2027)\n \n\n\n"
}
